  "nl_text": "The database schema named 'rschema_0403' comprises six tables: Student, Administrator, Book, Student_Borrow_Book, Student_Return_Book, and Administrator_Audit.\nThe Student table represents students, with columns for Contact_Number (VARCHAR(255)), Email (VARCHAR(255)), Grade (INTEGER), Major (VARCHAR(255)), Name (VARCHAR(255)), and Student_ID (INTEGER) as primary keys.\nThe Administrator table holds information about administrators, including Administrator_ID (INTEGER), Contact_Number (VARCHAR(255)), Email (VARCHAR(255)), Job_Number (INTEGER), Name (VARCHAR(255)), and Position (VARCHAR(255)).\nThe Book table contains information about books, including Author (VARCHAR(255)), Book_ID (INTEGER), Borrowed_Quantity (INTEGER), Category (VARCHAR(255)), Publication_Date (DATETIME), Publisher (VARCHAR(255)), Stock_Quantity (INTEGER), and Title (VARCHAR(255)).\nThe Student_Borrow_Book table records the borrowing of books by students, with columns for Borrow_Date (DATETIME), Borrowed_Book_ID (INTEGER), Return_Date (DATETIME), Review_Status (VARCHAR(255)), and Student_ID (INTEGER). The primary key is a combination of Student_ID and Borrowed_Book_ID. The foreign keys are Borrowed_Book_ID referencing Book(Book_ID) and Student_ID referencing Student(Student_ID).\nThe Student_Return_Book table records the returning of books by students, with columns for Book_ID (INTEGER), Return_Date (DATETIME), Returned_Book_ID (INTEGER), Review_Status (VARCHAR(255)), and Student_ID (INTEGER). The primary key is a combination of Student_ID and Returned_Book_ID. The foreign keys are Returned_Book_ID referencing Book(Book_ID) and Student_ID referencing Student(Student_ID).\nFinally, the Administrator_Audit table records administrative actions, including Administrator_ID (INTEGER), Audit_Date (DATETIME), Audit_Result (VARCHAR(255)), Book_ID (INTEGER), Borrowing_Status (VARCHAR(255)). The primary key is a combination of Administrator_ID and Book_ID. The foreign keys are Administrator_ID referencing Administrator(Administrator_ID) and Book_ID referencing Book(Book_ID).",
  "gold_question": "Business Requirement Description:\nThe following describes a Library Management System. The system’s main features might include:\n1.Student Management: Includes adding, modifying, deleting, and querying student information. Each student has a Student ID, Name, Student Number, Grade, Major, Contact Number, and Email.\n2.Administrator Management: Includes adding, modifying, deleting, and querying administrator information. The administrator details include Administrator ID, Name, Job Number, Contact Number, Email, and Position.\n3.Book Management: Includes adding, modifying, deleting, and querying book information. Book details include Book ID, Title, Author, Publisher, Publication Date, Category, Stock Quantity, and Borrowed Quantity.\n4.Book Borrowing Management: Includes adding, modifying, deleting, and querying student borrowing records. The records include Student ID, Borrowed Book ID, Borrow Date, Return Date, and Review Status.\n5.Book Returning Management: Includes adding, modifying, deleting, and querying student returning records. The records include Student ID, Borrowed Book ID, Return Date, and Review Status.\n6.Audit Management: Administrators review book borrowing and returning actions. The audit includes Administrator ID, Book ID, Borrowing Status, Audit Date, and Audit Result.",
  "input_json": "/data/RSchema_ExpResults4/Experiment2/schema2text_deepseek/0403.json",
  "ddl": "-- Schema for database: rschema_0403\nCREATE TABLE `student` (\n  `student_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `contact_number` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `email` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `grade` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `major` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`student_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `administrator` (\n  `administrator_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `contact_number` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `email` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `job_number` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `position` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`administrator_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `book` (\n  `book_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `title` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `author` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `publisher` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `publication_date` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  `category` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `stock_quantity` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `borrowed_quantity` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`book_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `student_borrow_book` (\n  `student_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `borrowed_book_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `borrow_date` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  `return_date` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  `review_status` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`student_id`, `borrowed_book_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `student_borrow_book_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`student_id`) REFERENCES `student` (`student_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `student_borrow_book_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`borrowed_book_id`) REFERENCES `book` (`book_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `student_return_book` (\n  `student_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `returned_book_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `book_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `return_date` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  `review_status` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`student_id`, `returned_book_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `student_return_book_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`student_id`) REFERENCES `student` (`student_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `student_return_book_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`returned_book_id`) REFERENCES `book` (`book_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `administrator_audit` (\n  `administrator_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `book_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `audit_date` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  `audit_result` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `borrowing_status` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`administrator_id`, `book_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `administrator_audit_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`administrator_id`) REFERENCES `administrator` (`administrator_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `administrator_audit_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`book_id`) REFERENCES `book` (`book_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;",
